         <actor editor-id="Aslfur" />
         <actor editor-id="Benor" />
         <actor editor-id="Falion" />
         <actor editor-id="Gorm" />
         <actor editor-id="Hroggar" />
         <actor editor-id="IdgrodRavencrone" name="Idgrod Ravencrone">
            <!--
               I have most Jarls respond to "Can you help me find someone?" by 
               telling the player to ask the steward instead. I am notably *not* 
               having Idgrod Ravencrone do that. Morthal has small-town vibes, 
               and Idgrod is written to imply that she knows more than she lets 
               on. Allowing her to respond to the player's inquiries plays to 
               both ideas, suggesting that she keeps closer track of people than 
               one would expect.
            -->
